* dev_zero <dev_xor-eZNTXLQAfP4@public.gmane.org> [2004-11-09 18:54:38 +0100]:

> How should I really reply to emails coming from this
> mailinglist?
> I wonder because when I get replays from you, I
> sometimes get two of the same email. Because you send
> the email to my email address and a Cc to this
> mailinglist which I subscribe to. When I send replays
> should I send the email to the mailinglist or should I
> send the replay to the person who sent the email with
> the mailinglist-address as Cc?
 Do whatever you prefer, and ask people about your reply preferency.
Usually it is a policy and a good thing(?) to send private replies _and_
a Cc to the mailing list. For example if you send a private mail, then
other users/developers won't see that your problem is taken care of, or
simple mail list send would result a lost wood in the forest effect, so
your mail might be 'lost' in other mailing list mails.
 Sometimes this annoys me, but I like it more often the way it happens.
What's your taste?

